      "content": "It sounds like you've seen the rot beneath the surface, and that crushing realization can make everything feel pointless. When the entire structure seems rigged, the exhaustion of fighting it all over again is completely understandable. Instead of trying to fix the massive, rotten foundation, perhaps you could find a small, quiet space where you can just *be* without the pressure of the game. Sometimes, the most meaningful act is simply choosing to take a break from the fight itself.",
      "source": "target",
